---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Vetlas & our data policy"
  description="What Vetlas is, how we label every fact with a trust tier, and why there are no ads or paid placements. Free forever, built for India."
  canonical="/about/"
>
  <div class="container">
    <header class="page-head" style="text-align:center;margin-inline:auto">
      <span class="card-icon" style="margin:0 auto;width:3.5rem;height:3.5rem;border-radius:18px;background:var(--teal);color:#fff">
        <Icon name="paw" class="icon icon-xl" />
      </span>
      <h1 style="margin-top:1rem">About Vetlas</h1>
      <p style="margin-inline:auto">
        Vetlas is an independent, India-wide veterinary care decision-support tool — not a
        directory, not an ad platform. Our goal: when your pet is unwell, help you choose the right
        care quickly, with attributed and trustworthy data.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="doc" style="margin-top:2.5rem;padding-bottom:1rem">
      <div class="doc-block">
        <h2><Icon name="badge" class="icon icon-lg" /> Our data policy</h2>
        <p>
          Every fact on Vetlas carries a <strong>trust label</strong> with a distinct geometric
          shape and colour:
        </p>
        <p style="display:grid;gap:0.5rem;margin-top:0.9rem">
          <span><strong>Verified</strong> — credentials checked by hand by the Vetlas team, with the date checked shown.</span>
          <span><strong>Provider-confirmed</strong> — details claimed and confirmed directly by the provider.</span>
          <span><strong>Public source</strong> — from public web pages, maps or directories, with fetch date and link.</span>
          <span><strong>User-submitted</strong> — moderated reports from pet owners.</span>
          <span><strong>Estimated</strong> — system-calculated ranges, shown only above minimum sample sizes.</span>
        </p>
        <p>
          Right now, while we're in beta, all records are <strong>sample data</strong> — realistic
          fictional content built to design and test the experience. Ratings, reviews, phone
          numbers and prices are illustrative only. We never invent provider information, reviews,
          ratings or pricing, and we never present sample data as real. Missing data is shown as
          "not available yet" — never guessed.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-block">
        <h2><Icon name="shield" class="icon icon-lg" /> No ads, no paid placement</h2>
        <p>
          Providers cannot pay for higher rankings or to hide reviews. Results follow data —
          trust level, review themes and fees — never money. Vetlas is free to use, forever.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-block">
        <h2><Icon name="sparkle" class="icon icon-lg" /> Themes over stars</h2>
        <p>
          A number out of five hides more than it shows. Vetlas surfaces recurring qualitative
          themes from reviews — like <em>"Calm with nervous pets"</em> — alongside ratings, so you
          can see <strong>how</strong> a place treats animals, not just how much.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-block">
        <h2><Icon name="clock" class="icon icon-lg" /> Built for the hard days</h2>
        <p>
          Most people find a vet for the first time during an emergency. Vetlas is optimised for
          that moment: fast search, 24×7 filters, fee transparency and a clear path to the right
          speciality. No popups, no lead-capture walls, no sponsored cards.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-block">
        <h2>Suggest a provider</h2>
        <p>
          Community submissions open soon. If you'd like to flag a great clinic or doctor — or
          correct something you see — the repository is public and issues are welcome.
        </p>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" style="margin-top:1rem" href="/search/">Start exploring</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
